extends ../../webinc/html/disease.jade

block head
    title Rectocele - Plants Cause Disease

block content
    h1 Rectocele
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://fascrs.org/patients/diseases-and-conditions/a-z/rectocele") American Society of Colon &amp; Rectal Surgeons]:
    blockquote A rectocele is a bulging of the front wall of the rectum into the back wall of the vagina. The rectum is the bottom section of your colon (large intestine). This is a very common problem that often does not produce symptoms. Other pelvic organs can bulge into the vagina, including the bladder (cystocele) and the small intestines (enterocele), producing similar problems.